title: Example - Markdown link - internal tiddler
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Markdown

The [LINK marker](#vocab/markdown/LINK) implements the TW markdown plugin's link syntax. `#` prefix is required for internal tiddler references (the marker has `link-hash-prefix: required`); targets without `#` (and not URL-shaped) are routed through `<a href>` as external/relative URLs. All five forms below render as working internal links via the `<$link>` widget.

## 1 — `#` prefix, no spaces in the target

[link text](#vocab/markdown/LINK)

```
[link text](#vocab/markdown/LINK)
```

The `#` is stripped at parse time and the rest is `decodeURIComponent`-ed (so `%20` becomes a space, `%29` a `)`, etc.). The clean tiddler title is then handed to `<$link to>`.

## 2 — URL-encoded spaces

[link text](#Vocabulary%20Engine)

```
[link text](#Vocabulary%20Engine)
```

`%20` is the standard URL encoding for a space. After `#`-strip and decode the target resolves to the `Vocabulary Engine` tiddler.

## 3 — Angle-bracket wrap for literal spaces and `<`/`>`

[link text](<#Vocabulary Engine>)

```
[link text](<#Vocabulary Engine>)
```

`<...>` accepts literal whitespace, no encoding needed. Inside the wrap, `\<` and `\>` unescape to literal angle brackets — so titles like `<$list>` can be referenced as `<#How to use \<$list\>>`.

## 4 — Trailing `"tooltip"` parameter

[link text](#Vocabulary Engine "Click to open the engine docs")

[link text](<#Vocabulary Engine> "Click to open the engine docs")

```
[link text](#Vocabulary Engine "Click to open the engine docs")

[link text](<#Vocabulary Engine> "Click to open the engine docs")
```

A whitespace-separated `"..."` after the target becomes the `tooltip` attribute on the rendered `<$link>` widget (which TW emits as the `<a title>` attribute). Hover the link to see it. Works with or without the `<...>` wrap.

## 5 — Empty body

[](<#vocab/markdown/LINK> "Empty body, the link still works")

```
[](<#vocab/markdown/LINK> "Empty body, the link still works")
```

Empty body produces a zero-width anchor — mostly useful for HTML-level anchor targets, less so for prose.

## How the engine assembles all this

[vocab/markdown/LINK](#vocab/markdown/LINK) sets four marker fields that, together, implement TW-md-plugin compatibility:

- `link-hash-prefix: required` — `#` triggers the internal route; bare targets fall through to external.
- `link-angle-brackets: yes` — accepts `<...>` wrapping with `\<` / `\>` escapes inside.
- `link-tooltip-attribute: tooltip` — peels off the trailing `"..."` and emits its content on this attribute.
- `auto-external: yes` — URL-shaped non-`#`-prefixed targets route through `<a href target="_blank">`.

The parser strips each affordance in turn (tooltip → angle-bracket → `#`-strip + decode) before applying `auto-external` and `link-attribute`. The final value handed to `<$link to>` is a clean tiddler title.

